  "notes": {
    "s_access": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "page": "access",
      "text": "Ways in: (1) the first admin signs up and creates the household; (2) everyone else joins by an invite link or QR code, already tied to a role and a person; (3) returning users sign in with a password or a one-time email link. Setup asks only for names and, for people who track macros, one line of numbers. Everything else is assumed and asked later — one tap-to-answer question per day.",
      "w": 620,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 980
    },
    "s_admin": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "page": "admin",
      "text": "Block = the account stays but cannot sign in; all sessions end immediately; reversible. Remove = the login is deleted from the household; the person as an eater (their plates, targets, reviews) can be kept or archived. Nothing here can be done to the last remaining admin.",
      "w": 620,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1300
    },
    "s_agent": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "page": "agent",
      "text": "Two kinds of change cards: 'Applied' (you asked for it — Undo is one tap) and 'Proposal' (the assistant's own idea — nothing changes until you Accept). Allergy removals, looser tolerances, removing people and role changes are always proposals, even if you asked.",
      "w": 620,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1220
    },
    "s_custom": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "page": "custom",
      "text": "One control everywhere: Basic · Detailed · Expert in each section's corner, per section and per person. Automatic values are always visible with an 'auto' tag; tap one to set it yourself, 'back to auto' undoes it. Lowering the level asks: keep your changes working quietly, or reset.",
      "w": 620,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1520
    },
    "s_plans": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "page": "plans",
      "text": "Sample numbers: Omar 2150 kcal · 180P/200C/70F; Sara 1655 kcal · 130P/160C/55F; Layla (18), Adam (15), Zayd (10, sesame allergy) have no targets. The same hammour is grilled for the adults and breaded-fried for the kids — same ingredients, different macros.",
      "w": 620,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1620
    },
